  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies the loss landscape of variational quantum classifiers by computing Hessian eigenvalues during training. Experiments are performed via PennyLane simulations on (1) a 4‑qubit parity classification circuit with 36 trainable parameters trained for ~100 iterations and (2) an 8‑qubit VQC applied to the Pima Indians Diabetes dataset with training shown for ~30 iterations. Results focus on curvature visualization and convergence behavior rather than accuracy or quantum speedup.",
